title: Lists and grids that lay themselves out
intro: A Layout lines up an entity's children in a list, a row or a grid. Spawn a card into it and it takes its place; destroy one and the rest close up. With Clip, what doesn't fit is cut off and the mouse wheel scrolls it.
project: Empty | Contract Board

chapter: A board of cards | Laid out in the Scene view
agent: entity_create {"entity": {"name": "Board", "components": {"Sprite": {"tint": "#2E3440", "size": [7, 5]}}}}
look: 0, 0, 4
say: Here's a board for a factory game's offers: just a dark sprite for now.
select: Board
add: Layout
set: Layout.Direction = Grid
set: Layout.Columns = 3
set: Layout.Size = 7, 5
set: Layout.Padding = 0.3
set: Layout.Spacing = 0.3
agent: entity_create {"parent": "Board", "entities": [{"name": "Card 1", "components": {"Sprite": {"tint": "#E0B040", "size": [1.6, 2], "order": 1}}}, {"name": "Card 2", "components": {"Sprite": {"tint": "#D08A50", "size": [1.6, 2], "order": 1}}}, {"name": "Card 3", "components": {"Sprite": {"tint": "#C06A70", "size": [1.6, 2], "order": 1}}}, {"name": "Card 4", "components": {"Sprite": {"tint": "#8A7AC0", "size": [1.6, 2], "order": 1}}}]}
expectat: Card 1 = -2.4, 1.2
expectat: Card 2 = -0.5, 1.2
expectat: Card 4 = -2.4, -1.1
explain: scene | Placed by the layout | Four cards were added inside the board with no positions at all. The Layout puts them in a grid of three columns, from its top left corner, with padding round the edge and spacing between them.
select: Board
explain: label:Layout.Direction | Vertical, Horizontal or Grid | Direction says which way they go: down a list, across a row, or in a grid. Each card takes the room of its sprite, or of its button, or a fixed Cell Size.

chapter: In the game | Spawned cards take their places
write: Scripts/Dealer.cs | layouts/Dealer.cs
code: Assets/Scripts/Dealer.cs | Dealer.cs
say: This script deals a card into the board with Space and takes the first one away with Backspace. It never sets a position.
hidecode
select: Board
add: Dealer
play
wait: 1
tap: Space
wait: 0.5
tap: Space
wait: 0.5
explain: game | Dealt in order | Each card spawned into the board goes after the last.
tap: Backspace
wait: 0.5
explain: game | The gap closes | Destroy one, and the rest move up to close the gap.
stop

chapter: More than fit | Clip and scroll
select: Board
set: Layout.Clip = true
set: Layout.Size = 7, 2.6
explain: scene | Cut at its edges | With Clip ticked, the cards that don't fit the layout's size are cut off at its edges, in the Scene view and in the game alike. Over the board, the mouse wheel scrolls it a row at a time, and the turn of the wheel isn't the world's.
say: Lists of contracts, offer boards, inventories and shop shelves no longer need a script to place every row.
